												<div id="earlyAccessHeader" class="early_access_header">
		<div class="heading">
												<h2 class="inset">Early Access Game</h2>
					<p class="inset subtitle">Get instant access and start playing; get involved with this game as it develops.</p>
				
				<p><span>Note:</span> Games in Early Access are not complete and may or may not change further. If you are not excited to play this game in its current state, then you
									should wait to see if the game progresses further in development. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/earlyaccessfaq/?snr=1_5_9_">Learn more</a></p>
					</div>
				<div id="earlyAccessBody" class="devnotes">
							<div class="devs_say">What the developers have to say:</div>
			
			<div id="devnotes_expander">
									<h3>Why Early Access?</h3>
					“Geoplanetical aims to become a benchmark for deep geopolitical simulation games. <br />
<br />
Its interconnected political, economic, social, diplomatic and military systems make community feedback especially valuable, as many aspects can only be properly evaluated through long and varied campaigns.<br />
<br />
Releasing in Early Access was not my original plan or usual approach. However, Geoplanetical has always been developed in close collaboration with its community, and 100% of respondents to a recent community poll asked for an Early Access release.<br />
<br />
The game’s core is already playable, major bugs are rare, and the save system and debugging pipeline are reliable. Early Access therefore feels like the right opportunity to involve players more directly while continuing to improve the depth, balance, accessibility and stability of the simulation.”
					<h3>Approximately how long will this game be in Early Access?</h3>
					“I currently expect Geoplanetical to remain in Early Access for approximately 18 to 24 months.<br />
<br />
This is only an estimate and may change depending on community feedback and the needs of development. My priority is to build a stable, coherent and genuinely deep geopolitical simulation rather than rush toward an arbitrary deadline.”
					<h3>How is the full version planned to differ from the Early Access version?</h3>
					“I plan to deepen the existing systems and expand the interactions between politics, economics, society, diplomacy, warfare and the evolution of the wider world.<br />
<br />
The exact direction will evolve according to testing, technical priorities and community feedback. The ambition is for Geoplanetical to become one of the genre’s reference points for players looking for a deep and large-scale geopolitical simulation.”
					<h3>What is the current state of the Early Access version?</h3>
					“The core experience of Geoplanetical is already playable. Players can begin a campaign as a playable terrestrial authority, explore the 3D globe and manage their country through interconnected political, economic, budgetary, social, diplomatic and military systems.<br />
<br />
The rest of the world continues to evolve through simulation and decisions made by other actors. Saving and loading are functional, major bugs are rare, and the project has a reliable debugging and testing pipeline.<br />
<br />
However, some systems still need further balancing, depth and accessibility. Players should expect bugs, incomplete areas and potentially significant changes throughout Early Access.”
					<h3>Will the game be priced differently during and after Early Access?</h3>
					“I plan to gradually increase the price as substantial content and features are added and Geoplanetical moves closer to its full release.<br />
<br />
Any planned price change will be communicated to the community in advance.”
					<h3>How are you planning on involving the Community in your development process?</h3>
					“Community involvement is at the heart of Geoplanetical’s development. <br />
<br />
Players already contribute through discussions, suggestions, bug reports and polls. <br />
<br />
The decision to consider Early Access itself came directly from the community, with 100% of respondents to the poll supporting it.<br />
<br />
I intend to continue listening closely to feedback, sharing development progress and explaining major changes. Community reports will help identify priorities, improve balancing and usability, and reveal issues that only emerge during long campaigns.<br />
<br />
This collaboration will help shape the development process while preserving the project’s central vision: making Geoplanetical a deep, ambitious and distinctive reference within the geopolitical simulation genre.”
							</div> <!-- /devnotes_expander -->
			<a class="morebutton" id="devnotes_more" href="#"  onclick="$J('#devnotes_expander').css({'max-height': 'none'}); $J(this).hide(); return false;">Read more</a>
		</div>
	</div>
										
					
